; Generated by `tatami -o schema`, and compiled: the loaders call `Repo.make`
; and the getters, so the modules have to be real rather than stand-ins.
;
; Unwrapped because the generated code names its neighbours directly --
; `Run.repo_id : Repo.id` -- and a wrapping prefix would be a name the
; generator has no reason to know about.
;
; The .mli here are also read at run time, as data, by Tatami.Schema.load_dir.
; That still works: dune copies the sources into the build directory, and the
; loaders deliberately have no .mli, so the reader sees four tables and not
; nine.
(library
 (name rows)
 (wrapped false)
 (libraries shred yojson pgx))
